## Workflow

This repository uses the shared **arbisoft-workflows** commands, configured in
`.claude/workflow.json` (project) and `.claude/workflow.local.json` (personal, git-ignored).

| Step | Command | Writes to tracker? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Pick | `/pick-ticket` | no |
| Several at once | `/parallel-tickets [KEY ...]` | no (each worktree session runs `/start-ticket`) |
| Open | `/start-ticket <KEY>` | Planned SP (asked), → In Progress, cuts the branch |
| Analyse / plan | `/analyze-ticket`, `/plan`, `/plan-review` | no |
| Build | `/implement` | no |
| Review | `/self-review`, `/perf-check` | no |
| Ship | `/create-pr` | → Code Review |
| After review | `/pr-comments` | no |
| Record | `/ai-contribution`, `/log-failure` | no |

Rules: never move a ticket backwards; never invent story points; failed tracker calls are
reported, never folded into success. Plans live in `<plans.dir>`; AI corrections go in
`<failureLog.path>`.

## Before writing code

1. Read the file you are modifying.
2. Check whether a similar component / helper / pattern already exists.
3. Verify every import, key, endpoint, and prop you reference actually exists.
4. Consider the runtime cost at production scale, not on your laptop.
